# THE RING AT NIGHT (19_orbit, src/render/orbit/): a pass staged overhead at
# half past midnight, deep in the Earth's shadow. It is lit only by its own lamps
# -- the cold rows with their dead runs, the hub's beacon, the wound's embers --
# and the stars go out behind the hull (`ring_hides_stars`, asked of the live
# frame: the dark hull's pixels asked in a frame with the ring and one a few
# frames later with its layer held off).
#   TOUR_FIXED_FPS=60 tools/tour.sh tours/orbit_night.tour --seed=7 --place=coast --hour=0.5 --orbit=zenith@0.5 --eye=1.7,-80,70 --face=146 --weather=clear:0
wait 2
# The clock ran while the world warmed up; put it back where the pass is staged.
hour 0.5
wait 1
await ring_eclipsed 5
await ring_hides_stars 10
shot 00-eclipsed
wait 3
shot 01-eclipsed-moving
